     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Confirming it doesn't change the risk. A single 4,000 mg dose is above the toxic threshold for ibuprofen (about 400 mg/kg is severe, and 100 mg/kg can already cause symptoms). For a 70 kg patient, 4,000 mg is about 57 mg/kg per dose, and four doses would total 16,000 mg/day. I know of no indication that calls for this, and it would likely cause serious harm.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg by mouth four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf the goal is stronger pain or inflammation control, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead. Tell me which drugs and doses you want.\n\nIf I've misread the order, for example if the intended unit or drug was different, tell me and I'll correct it."
      }
     ],
